{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794163384","published":"2026-11-08T18:43:16Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:17:20.197760527Z","upstream":["CVE-2024-0397","CVE-2024-4032","CVE-2026-1299"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2024-0397, CVE-2024-4032, CVE-2026-1299","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: race condition in ssl.SSLContext.cert_store_stats()\n     and get_ca_certs()\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-0397.patch: in Modules/_ssl.c, take a locked\n       copy of the X509_STORE object list (shim of OpenSSL 3.3's\n       X509_STORE_get1_objects()) instead of iterating the live list, so a\n       concurrent certificate load can no longer free entries while they are\n       read. Backport of upstream commit 29c97287d205 (gh-114572, 3.8\n       branch); the get_ca_certs() failure path releases the result list,\n       as in the original 3.12 fix.\n     - CVE-2024-0397\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: incorrect \"private\"/\"global\" classification of IP\n     address ranges\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-4032.patch: in Lib/ipaddress.py, update the\n       is_private / is_global tables to the IANA special-purpose registries\n       and handle IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses. Backport of upstream commit\n       895f7e2ac23e (gh-113171, 3.8 branch); the Doc/whatsnew/3.8.rst hunk\n       is dropped. Bundles the upstream regression tests.\n     - CVE-2024-4032\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: email header injection through BytesGenerator\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-1299.patch: in Lib/email/generator.py, apply\n       the verify_generated_headers checks in BytesGenerator._write_headers()\n       too. Backport of upstream commit 052e55e7d447 (gh-144125), with\n       bytes.removesuffix() replaced by slicing. Bundles the upstream\n       regression tests.\n     - debian/patches/bpo-34424.patch, debian/patches/gh-142006.patch:\n       prerequisites of the BytesGenerator header check. In\n       Lib/email/_header_value_parser.py, strip the whole policy.linesep\n       when refolding an encoded word (upstream c0abd0c8e9b6, bpo-34424),\n       so smtplib.send_message() no longer raises HeaderWriteError, and drop\n       an empty line left in the fold buffer (upstream 90ca216cdcb7,\n       gh-142006).\n     - CVE-2026-1299","affected":[{"package":{"name":"idle-python3.6","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/idle-python3.6?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.9-1~18.04ubuntu1.12+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1794163384.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.6","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpython3.6?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.9-1~18.04ubuntu1.12+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1794163384.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.6-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpython3.6-dev?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.9-1~18.04ubuntu1.12+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1794163384.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.6-minimal","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpython3.6-minimal?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.9-1~18.04ubuntu1.12+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1794163384.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.6-stdlib","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpython3.6-stdlib?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.9-1~1